<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paxos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Paxi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paxos is a small island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a>, south of Corfu, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Under Venetian rule for centuries, it became part of the Septinsular Republic in 1800 and later of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of the Ionian Islands. With the other islands it was united with Greece in 1864.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paxos.jpg" alt="Paxos" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagai Agmon-Snir حچاي اچمون-سنير חגי אגמון-שניר · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GaiosPaxiJuly192022_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
